{"title":"Ddk001","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>If you have a problem or solution to contribute, please go to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Problems_Collection\" title=\"Problems Collection\">this page</a>.\n</p><p><br />\nI am a aops user who likes making and doing problems, doing math, and redirecting pages (see <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Principle_of_Insufficient_Reasons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Principle of Insufficient Reasons\">Principle of Insufficient Reasons</a>). I like geometry and don't like counting and probability. My number theory skill are also not bad\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<div style=\"border:2px solid black; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; background:#F0F2F3\">\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"User_Count\"><font color=\"black\" style=\"font-family: ITC Avant Garde Gothic Std, Verdana\"><div style=\"margin-left:10px\">User Count</div></font></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: User Count\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<div style=\"margin-left: 10px; margin-bottom:10px\"><font color=\"black\">If this is your first time visiting this page, edit it by incrementing the user count below by one.</font></div>\n<center><font size=\"100px\">59</font></center>\n<div style=\"margin-left: 10px; margin-bottom:10px\"><font color=\"black\">Please do not mess with the user count. I would know and I would find you. Apparently I do have to add this last sentence. </font></div>\n</div>\n<p>Credits given to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Firebolt360\" title=\"User:Firebolt360\">Firebolt360</a> for inventing the box above. But do you? -InterstellarXYk\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Scores\">Scores</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Scores\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"2022\">2022</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: 2022\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>AMC 10A 91.5 (I think)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"2023\">2023</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: 2023\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>AMC 12A 102\n</p><p>AMC 12B 99\n</p><p>AIME Qual (Score = 7)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"2024\">2024</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: 2024\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Quitted competition for a year\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"2025\">2025</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: 2025\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>AMC 12A: 129 \n</p><p>AMC 10B: 109.5 \n</p><p>AIME Score: 10 (I guessed #14 correctly)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Cool_asyptote_graphs\">Cool asyptote graphs</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Cool asyptote graphs\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Asymptote is fun!\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d61604256e9de426afc94111a204811ff9d3cf0e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]draw((0,0)----(0,6));draw((0,-3)----(-3,3));draw((3,0)----(-3,6));draw((6,-6)----(-6,3));draw((6,0)----(-6,0));[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d78519cbbf9c22e2c4ea74ee089557db7a04e2ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]draw(circle((0,0),1));draw((1,0)----(0,1));draw((1,0)----(0,2));draw((0,-1)----(0,2));draw(circle((0,3),2));draw(circle((0,4),3));draw(circle((0,5),4));draw(circle((0,2),1));draw((0,9)----(0,18));[/asy]\" width=\"78\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Contributions\">Contributions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Contributions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"AMC\">AMC</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: AMC\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23</a> Solution 7\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25</a> Solution 6\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20</a> Solution 3\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"AIME\">AIME</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: AIME\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 14</a> Solution 4\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 10</a> Solution 3\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 14</a> Solution 2\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">2019 AIME I Problems/Problem 15</a> Solution 6\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 3</a> Solution 3\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 5</a> Solution 2\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 12</a> Solution 1\n</p><p>Restored diagram for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">1994 AIME Problems/Problem 7</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"USAMO.2FUSAJMO\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"USAMO/USAJMO\">USAMO/USAJMO</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: USAMO/USAJMO\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">1973 USAMO Problems/Problem 2</a> Solution 3\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 1</a> Solution 4\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 2</a> Solution 2\n</p><p>Restored solution for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">2022 USAMO Problems/Problem 6</a> Solution 1     \nSee <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=history\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=history</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"IMO\">IMO</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: IMO\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">1961 IMO Problems/Problem 3</a> Solution 3 \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">1976 IMO Problems/Problem 6</a> Solution 2\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">1978 IMO Problems/Problem 4</a> Solution 1\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">1986 IMO Problems/Problem 3</a> Solution 2 \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">1995 IMO Problems/Problem 6</a> Solution 1\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Theorems\">Theorems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Theorems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divergence_Theorem\" title=\"Divergence Theorem\">Divergence Theorem</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stokes%27_Theorem\" title=\"Stokes&#39; Theorem\">Stokes' Theorem</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Principle_of_Insufficient_Reasons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Principle of Insufficient Reasons\">Principle of Insufficient Reasons</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem\" title=\"The Nested Sum Theorem\">The Nested Sum Theorem</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hensel%27s_Lemma\" title=\"Hensel&#39;s Lemma\">Hensel's Lemma</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definitions\">Definitions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Definitions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Laplace_Transform\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Laplace Transform\">Laplace Transform</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial_Congruences\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Polynomial Congruences\">Polynomial Congruences</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Primitive_Roots\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Primitive Roots\">Primitive Roots</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Order_of_a_integer&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Order of a integer (page does not exist)\">Order of a integer</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Index\" title=\"Index\">Index</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diagonalizability\" title=\"Diagonalizability\">Diagonalizability</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Others\">Others</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Others\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Proofs_to_Some_Number_Theory_Facts\" title=\"Proofs to Some Number Theory Facts\">Proofs to Some Number Theory Facts</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chebyshev_and_the_history_of_the_Prime_Number_Theorem\" title=\"Chebyshev and the history of the Prime Number Theorem\">Chebyshev and the history of the Prime Number Theorem</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Proof_of_the_Existence_of_Primitive_Roots\" title=\"Proof of the Existence of Primitive Roots\">Proof of the Existence of Primitive Roots</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Proof_of_Some_Primitive_Roots_Facts&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Proof of Some Primitive Roots Facts (page does not exist)\">Proof of Some Primitive Roots Facts</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems_Sharing_Contest\">Problems Sharing Contest</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problems Sharing Contest\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Here, you can post all the math problems that you have. Everyone will try to come up with a appropriate solution. The person with the first solution will post the next problem. I'll start:\n</p><p>1. There is one and only one perfect square in the form\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11bf3dce41593092737df0eea5f902de3989389.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p^2+1)(q^2+1)-((pq)^2-pq+1)\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are prime. Find that perfect square. ~<a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Ddk001</a>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/c/abc42babe799a8446eee2d9d4b05f3c00c9e59ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Solution by cxsmi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>1. We can expand the product in the expression. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792e3ae11abf253939a51255b628ea111c2d4307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p^2+1)(q^2+1)-((pq)^2-pq+1) = p^2q^2+p^2+q^2+1-((pq)^2-pq+1) = p^2 + q^2 + pq$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"705\" height=\"21\" />. Suppose this equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f521656db779d024e6aff0f9a3771ac28d2c3db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. We rewrite using the square of a binomial pattern to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cc6002ba91aff3db241c9ade576beffce53804d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 = (p + q)^2 - pq$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"21\" />. Through trial and error on small values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in some order. The perfect square formed using these numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421fc4dd92b07b768ba57f5e489e184f57c0048d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{49}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Note: I will be the first to admit that this solution is somewhat lucky.\n</p><p><br />\n2. A diamond is created by connecting the points at which a square circumscribed around the incircle of an isosceles right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> itself. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has leg length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. The perimeter of this diamond is expressible as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/7/7a710ff759753fcf79c3176e8d1e93eddefc2d7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\sqrt{b}-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. What is the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf4b2b8da31fb32285d5b573ffbb35e870afea4c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1inch); draw((0,0)--(0,2)); draw((0,2)--(2,0)); draw((2,0)--(0,0)); draw(circle((0.586,0.586),0.586)); draw((0,0)--(0,1.172),red); draw((0,1.172)--(1.172,1.172)); draw((1.172,1.172)--(1.172,0)); draw((1.172,0)--(0,0),red); draw((0,1.172)--(0.828,1.172),red); draw((0.828,1.172)--(1.172,0.828),red); draw((1.172,0.828)--(1.172,0),red); draw((0,0.1)--(0.1,0.1)); draw((0.1,0.1)--(0.1,0)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,2.1)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(0,-0.1)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(2,-0.1)); label(&quot;$2024$&quot;,(-0.2,1)); label(&quot;$2024$&quot;,(1,-0.2)); [/asy]\" width=\"298\" height=\"295\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7a5de90fd7578c7232ba2cd62ab1becf87d886.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Solution by Ddk001}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The inradius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d5d23a7e91fb9f6c248fb4cd43111165540f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, can be calculated as \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d02fa3396a9eff50f834c674242087b858095775.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=\\frac{\\textbf{Area}_{ABC}}{\\textbf{Semiperimeter}} \\implies r=\\frac{2024^2/2}{(2024+2024+2024 \\sqrt{2})/2}=\\frac{2024}{2+\\sqrt{2}}=2024-1012\\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"675\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>so the square have side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/804aa5b9751bbfead8503a9f4a82269837339795.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4048-2024 \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"21\" />. Let the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the vertex of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/0529c20d792fb680e498c1de5f8f84389b9bfa58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D \\ne B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/4/684a22b1a6c2431286d047461468f3843b34b0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC= 2024 (\\sqrt{2} -1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"24\" />. Let the sides of the square intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3de28a7a2295c7d5273be69e92b135c217d630de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE&lt;AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8da05c648d761fcc63f3776bf85b4d31017a90c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=CF=2024(2-\\sqrt{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"24\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb5c04e02829566cba5f85e2e2644dd9899be1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=2024 (3 \\sqrt{2} -4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"24\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the vertex of the square across from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d59a8e3be4d5a87a258d308691fa2c84cce8199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG=FG=2024 (3-2\\sqrt{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"223\" height=\"24\" />. Thus the perimeter of the diamond is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc8e18a5b46de191c8436a2d6d363517962ce15f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4(4048-2024 \\sqrt{2})-2 \\cdot 2024 (3-2\\sqrt{2})+2024 (3 \\sqrt{2} -4)=2024 (8-4 \\sqrt{2}-6+4\\sqrt{2}+3\\sqrt{2}-4)=2024(3\\sqrt{2}-2)=7072\\sqrt{2}-4048\\]\" width=\"928\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>The desired sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/478e806e642fa9187af2f93de6b9454f7467c2e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7072+2+4048=\\boxed{11122}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"209\" height=\"25\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Ddk001</a> Presents\n</p><p><br />\nTHE FOLLOWING PROBLEM\n</p><p>Note: This is one of my favorite problems. Very well designed and actually used two of my best tricks without looking weird.\n</p><p>Suppose\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a4c33ddcd46bcf5c89a3e3115bc73c2c9c5d3d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x \\equiv 2^4 \\cdot 3^4 \\cdot 7^4+2^7 \\cdot 3^7 \\cdot 5^6 \\pmod{7!}\\]\" width=\"293\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bba398d446dc3d6c6e32a464aeefc92e8eb19385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by 1000.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/b/aebcaa2c686b5752121f7d78c2ffde12f1050384.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\equiv 0\\pmod{2^4}, x\\equiv 0\\pmod{3^2}\\]\" width=\"273\" height=\"20\" /> Also, by FLT, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/3/3f3b052203e7a74b5d7cbd74605abf2c1bf02c61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\equiv 1\\cdot 1\\cdot 1+0\\equiv 3 \\pmod{5} \\text{ and } x\\equiv 2+3+1\\equiv 6 \\pmod{7}\\]\" width=\"493\" height=\"18\" /> Using CRT, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/3302351e35682e97daf6a014e7be2b0e253b2d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\equiv 13\\pmod{35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e3e790ab6e887b169157585b4ec60c5e6062b88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13\\cdot 2^4\\cdot 3^2 = 1\\boxed{872}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"151\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~sillybone\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Vandalism_area\">Vandalism area</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Vandalism area\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Congratulations! You had reached the end of this boring user page. Time for vandalism! Write anything under 45000 bytes.\nHi Ddk001 ~ zhenghua\n</p><p>Today my math teacher at school thought that a triangle had to be equilateral just because an altitude could be drawn in it and graded my homework 90% because the wrong answer was correct....\n(Wait can't any triangle have an altitude?)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vandalism_Page&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Vandalism Page (page does not exist)\">Vandalism Page</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>My <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User_talk:Ddk001\" title=\"User talk:Ddk001\">talk page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Problems_Collection\" title=\"Problems Collection\">My problems collection</a></li></ul>\n<p>The problems on this page are NOT copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>'s <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://amc.maa.org\">American Mathematics Competitions</a>. <span class=\"mw-default-size mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/8b/AMC_logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"92\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\">\n<p>Can someone help me clear out <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Problem_Collection\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Problem Collection\">this page</a>?\n</p></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018082146\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.085 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 395/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser f